guide.academic_exams.title: Academic Exams
guide.admission.p1: An admission category is a real applicant route, and requirement profiles are the score variants inside it.
guide.admission.p2: Requirements are minimum thresholds. For safer planning, also compare yourself with average admitted scores.
guide.admission.p3: Mode any means one language proof is enough. Mode all means every listed proof is required.
guide.admission.p4: Scholarships and aid can noticeably reduce total cost, so always check the selected funding option.
guide.admission.title: How to read admission categories
guide.exam_basics.p1: Admissions usually need two parts: academic scores and proof of language proficiency.
guide.exam_basics.p2: Requirements differ by country, university, program, and requirement profile, so check the selected choice directly.
guide.exam_basics.p3: Language requirements are especially important for international programs.
guide.exam_basics.p4: Simple strategy: first cover minimums, then improve scores for stronger options.
